    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the unequivocal anchor of the offense. With a score of 78.97, his matchup against McGreevy (xERA 4.53) provides the ideal environment for the speed-first profile we covet; the combination of a favorable SP skill set and an assumed #3 slot in the order creates massive upside for both counting stats and stolen base potential. **Josh Naylor** (65.60) and **Gabriel Moreno** (61.42) round out our top-tier tier of plays, with **Josh Naylor** benefiting significantly from the matchup against Chandler, effectively leveraging his platoon advantage to bolster the RBI floor. **Tyler Soderstrom** also earns a strong recommendation (60.98) as his spot in the #4 hole maximizes his exposure to run-scoring opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today centered on **Seiya Suzuki** (53.53) versus the deeper bench options. While **Seiya Suzuki** carries a mediocre projection against the formidable Freddy Peralta, the algorithm opted to start him due to a unique statistical quirk: Peralta\u2019s notoriously slow delivery to the plate. Despite the BvP concerns, the marginal advantage in theft probability provided enough lift to keep **Seiya Suzuki** active over the rest of the bench. We are carefully monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Jose Caballero**, **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, and **Seiya Suzuki**; if any of these pieces slide down the order upon final confirmation, their scores\u2014particularly that of **James Wood** (52.59)\u2014could be subject to immediate downward revision given the difficulty of the matchup against S\u00e1nchez.\n\nRisks remain focused on the lower-rung starters like **Max Muncy** (45.36) and **Cole Young** (44.97). Both are hovering near our \"Below Floor\" threshold, primarily hindered by poor batting order placement and the need to conserve game caps for higher-leverage outings. We continue to track the health of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, whose continued presence on the IL limits our depth, while rotational depth pieces like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** remain on standby should late-day lineup shuffling necessitate a pivot. Proceed with confidence in the top half of the order, but keep a watchful eye on the wind and weather reports for the early afternoon games.",
